# 105. Artemis Conversational Maturity Roadmap

Conversational maturity must advance by evidence.

It is independent from both Autonomous Operations maturity in Section 85 and
automated-trading maturity in Section 53.

## Conversation Stage C0 — Shell

- Chat UI exists
- No claim of real Artemis integration
- No privileged action

## Conversation Stage C1 — Truthful Read Assistant

- Authenticated read-only inspection
- Canonical capability awareness
- Page context
- No mutation

## Conversation Stage C2 — Explain and Report

- Decision/action history is grounded in canonical ledgers
- WHY and SHOW_EVIDENCE work
- User/admin reports are truthful

## Conversation Stage C3 — Plan and Proposal

- Natural-language goals compile to canonical plans and Action Intents
- Diffs and approval previews are real
- No autonomous material write

## Conversation Stage C4 — Human-Approved Action

- Approved conversational actions execute through canonical tools
- Trusted approval UX, verification and audit are operational

## Conversation Stage C5 — Autonomous Low-Risk Operation

- Proven O1 and selected O2 actions may be initiated conversationally
- Human locks, rollback and Kill Switch are operational
- Capability truthfulness remains verified

## Conversation Stage C6 — Durable Task Delegation

- Long-running goals survive disconnect/restart
- Pause/resume/cancel work
- Authorization is revalidated
- Proactive progress/status is available

## Conversation Stage C7 — Delegated Domain Operator

- For explicitly mature domains, users can accomplish most ordinary workflows
  conversationally
- Artemis performs routine planning, execution and reporting inside delegated
  authority
- Exceptions escalate correctly

## Conversation Stage C8 — Primary TitanGold Interface

Artemis conversation may be considered the primary interface for approved
domains only when:

- Human users are not required to understand internal navigation for ordinary
  workflows
- Underlying canonical UI remains available
- Capability discovery is complete
- Operational and financial boundaries remain enforced
- The interface remains truthful during degraded and incomplete states
- Human QA confirms real usability

## 105.1 Domain-Specific Maturity

Conversation maturity may differ by domain.

Example:

- Agent analysis: C7
- Agent configuration: C5
- Data Hub source management: C3
- Admin operations: C4
- Live trading: C1 or blocked

Do not use one global conversational maturity label to hide incomplete domains.

## 105.2 No Maturity Leakage

Advancing conversational maturity does not:

- Grant operational autonomy
- Grant Live trading
- Increase financial limits
- Increase RBAC
- Remove approval requirements

Each maturity program remains independently governed.

